Today we released the code for our CVPR 2026 paper, Flowception. Flowception bridges fully bidirectional sequence modeling and autoregressive generation by inserting frames via learned order, then denoising them with continuous flow.

@__JohnNguyen__: "I thought the path to variable-length video was frame-wise autoregressive with complex forcing schedules, but I was wrong! The solution is simple! Flowception, using frame insertions to model any-order video generation." 

The linked paper presents a novel non-autoregressive and variable-length video generation framework that interleaves discrete frame insertions with continuous frame denoising.
